id: pmc-release-corrections
title: Preserve published claims with append-only release corrections
description: "Record explicitly linked post-publication factual corrections, preserving immutable milestone wording and exposing the correction chain in a current view. Overlap rechecked against CLI and sibling source: claim-audit validates before publication; pm-evidence owns source-fragment validity; core owns item history, annotations and transactional coordination. No existing release correction chain found."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: append-only,release-corrections
created_at: "2026-10-27T04:22:07.291Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T15:43:49.890Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Replay creates no duplicate correction; supersession cycle refuses; historical output remains byte-identical while a current view exposes original and corrected wording with evidence. Typed SDK and CLI, strict bounded inputs, compact TOON/JSON, non-git and real public-tracker validation, seeded model and concurrency proofs, packed npm/Bun acceptance and CI npm/Bun release gates."
comments[40]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T04:24:20.869Z",codex-agent,"Design: native SDK comments retain versioned correction envelopes; immutable milestone fingerprint plus predecessor revision binds replay identity. Core workspace transaction serializes chain changes, SDK annotation append-if-absent owns normalization/history. Each apply and retry re-reads the target through the SDK; historical generation is unchanged. Current view exposes original wording, each corrected wording and evidence. Malformed and foreign records are skipped independently. No item create/update or journaled multi-target plan is introduced."
  "2026-10-27T04:37:46.275Z",codex-agent,"SDK capability audit found native structured context events (notes addJson), which core treats as immutable and refuses to edit/delete. Corrections now use those events instead of mutable plain comments. Complete internal reads explicitly disable SDK row/token output compaction and enforce annotation/chain bounds; the seeded model exposed the earlier incomplete-read defect. Real public baseline validation: 202 items, 189 done-role items, 202 frozen members, 15130 historical bytes, 2 new corrections, replay 0, chain length 2, 29 native fields unchanged, source tree byte-identical. Source copy is filesystem read-only; mutations occur only in a disposable non-git overlay."
  "2026-10-27T04:42:11.530Z",codex-agent,"Out-of-scope finding recorded in pmc-milestone-status-roles: pre-existing immutable milestone generation compares the literal closed status. New correction reads use SDK terminal_done roles and work with custom registries; this change does not reinterpret historical generation."
  "2026-10-27T04:46:08.229Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only appendReleaseCorrection persistence with an unchanged read-only receipt makes the append/replay/chain regression fail (expected changed true, actual false; exit 1). Production source restored byte-for-byte. Final native-event model: seed 0x0c011ec7, 500 random-data operation sequences, 2500 operations, 500 SDK-read events, all pass; exact prose/CRLF, historical replays, relationships and ambient focus preserved. Real tracker source reads require a filesystem read-only source copy because SDK reads can populate operational caches; no source bytes changed in measured validation."
  "2026-10-27T04:51:11.090Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed: 6 installation modes (npm/Bun global, npm/Bun local, npx, bunx), 8 launcher paths including both global pm aliases, 32 behavioral checks and 8 linked corrections on one non-git tracker. Native JSON context events reject edits/deletion. Final property scheduler now shuffles append, older replay, stale attempt and JSON/TOON round-trip operations per sequence; CI will repeat 500 sequences at the exact pushed head. Local typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates are reserved for CI because of host load."
  "2026-10-27T04:54:28.461Z",codex-agent,"Final public-source native-event validation: 202 items, 189 done-role items, 202 milestone members; 15130 historical bytes unchanged (SHA256 d2b5ec65c64e3e79d15796486a78a211a900624a0bc45ce4f7e06bd2f5f7411e). Two corrections, replay zero, two-link chain; 28 native fields unchanged and the derived note count increases by exactly two. This supersedes the earlier 29-field measurement from the mutable-comment prototype. Source remains byte-identical and filesystem read-only; all writes stay in a disposable overlay. Compatibility/docs/pack-scan tests: 80 passed, 0 failed/skipped. Linked pm test: 11 passed, 0 failed/skipped. Transaction identity now uses the SDK deriveMutationTransactionId over the canonical target-bound record."
  "2026-10-27T04:59:36.302Z",codex-agent,"Review hardening for PR 291: the reference model now preserves complete prior SDK-read native event records as an exact prefix, including author, timestamps, text, format and event discriminator, in addition to every correction field and unchanged native relationships/scope/body. An 8-sequence/40-operation metadata probe passes; the committed model retains 500 randomized sequences/2500 operations for full CI. Concurrent identical requests now use distinct owner/peer author IDs at every successful transaction boundary. No product behavior changed."
  "2026-10-27T05:05:25.974Z",codex-agent,"Final bounded-state fix: append now refuses before writing when the current native annotation count is already 10000, so a successful append cannot itself make the current view exceed its documented bound. Exact replays still return unchanged at a full bound. Added the pure boundary regression plus direct registered source-handler execution/refusal coverage on a real SDK tracker. Focused peer-author, limit and source-host checks pass (3/3); no SDK substitution."
  "2026-10-27T05:13:12.102Z",codex-agent,"Boundary fuzzing now rejects trailing line terminators in identifiers/fingerprints, unsupported control characters and unpaired Unicode surrogates. A maximum-size valid emoji/Unicode record round-trips through actual UTF-8 JSON and TOON bytes. SDK view production validates the frozen original wording through the same schema before any append, so every produced view is renderable. Focused Unicode/schema/original-source checks pass (3/3). Verified that workspace transactions, structured mutation identity and immutable JSON notes already exist at the declared SDK peer floor; no dependency or runtime floor change is needed."
  "2026-10-27T05:20:31.964Z",codex-agent,"Complete focused verification on the final implementation: 14 tests passed, zero failed/skipped; release-corrections.ts and release-correction-command.ts each measure 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Added an explicit missing-required-fields input to boundary fuzzing. Existing compatibility/docs/pack checks remain 80 passed; packed acceptance remains 32 checks across 8 launchers and 6 installation modes. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates and the 500-sequence full metadata model will run in CI at the final pushed head; PR 291 records the exact run and counts."
  "2026-10-27T05:24:36.141Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the peer-floor capability note: native immutable JSON notes and workspace transactions exist at the old floor, but the generic deriveMutationTransactionId export does not exist in the old 2026.10.4 SDK source. Declared host and peer minima now match the verified 2026.10.23 SDK used by packed acceptance, with no development dependency pin bump. Manifest, package/lock metadata, README and exact-floor refusal regression are aligned; older hosts refuse before extension loading. Current CLI 2026.10.26 remains supported."
  "2026-10-27T06:09:01.022Z",codex-agent,"The initial full CI run for head 3eb3ffb passed npm and Bun gates on Node 22 and 26, plus direct Bun runtime smokes and CodeQL; Node 26 logs report 922 tests in each gate, zero failures/skips and 100 percent configured lines/branches/functions. Added the remaining four compensation-boundary peer interleavings to satisfy every observable transaction boundary: compensating, step_compensating, step_compensated and compensated. The focused regression passes on one non-git tracker with distinct owner/peer authors; peer returns unchanged and the single immutable assertion remains intact. Product implementation is unchanged; the final test head will repeat full CI."
  "2026-10-27T07:18:06.291Z",codex-agent,"Re-review rule: a published claim belongs to its earliest qualifying immutable capture, never an arbitrary later snapshot of the same item. Merged current main first and installed its updated pinned toolchain. Whole-package audit found correction view/append and tracker generation as independent attribution consumers; CLI/hosted commands and serializers must delegate to one chronological, registry-role-based claim ledger. This also addresses pmc-milestone-status-roles. The supplied review contains one blocking finding; GitHub inline review comments contain no additional findings. Existing remote reviewer quota/trial notices are not approvals."
  "2026-10-27T07:44:24.068Z",codex-agent,"Re-review class audit complete: release-corrections reader/append/recovery and tracker generation now share one chronological first-done-role ledger. Searched all milestone readers, membership selectors, SDK exports, standalone/host CLI, compact JSON/TOON, installed consumers and non-git paths; no independent later-capture attribution remains. The existing status-role follow-up is covered by the same ledger using the configured SDK registry; explicit generation status filters remain respected. Behavioral revert proof: restoring only the former correction reader makes the legacy later-snapshot regression fail (missing expected correction_missing rejection); restoring only unsorted catalog traversal makes the 500-permutation ownership test fail (b-reopen steals a-recapture). Both mutations were restored byte-for-byte. The original invalid-wording fixture now uses a fresh first-published item so it still tests the same refusal after ownership is enforced; no assertion was removed or weakened."
  "2026-10-27T07:54:12.795Z",codex-agent,"Final re-review local evidence: related focused set 42 passed, zero failures/skips/cancels; final first-publication regression file 4 passed after adding catalog name/fingerprint drift, also passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Public read-only validation: 202 items, 189 done-role items, 202 milestone members, 2 corrections, zero replay duplicates, chain length 2; 15130 historical bytes and source bytes unchanged, 28 native fields unchanged. Historical SHA256 d2b5ec65c64e3e79d15796486a78a211a900624a0bc45ce4f7e06bd2f5f7411e. Existing tests and coverage thresholds remain intact; full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI with at most two workers."
  "2026-10-27T07:56:38.027Z",codex-agent,"Packed re-review acceptance passed: 64 checks across 6 installation modes and 8 launcher paths (npm/Bun global and project-local, both global host aliases, npx and bunx); all 32 wrong-release JSON/TOON view/append checks refused, 8 owning-release corrections appended and exact replays created none. Main advanced again with the generated-dist lint configuration change; merged it before the fix commit without touching existing tracker history. Both the supplied blocker and the status-role follow-up are addressed; no additional concrete inline review findings were present."
  "2026-10-27T08:01:31.843Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local evidence are complete at 84dc631. CI release verification is running at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40470314900 (npm/Bun on Node 22 and 26, unchanged 100 percent configured thresholds, two workers). CodeQL passed at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40470314754. A tracker-only evidence/claim-release commit will trigger final-head verification; the authoritative final run URL and measured gate counts are maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. No merge or release is authorized. The supplied attribution blocker and the status-role follow-up are fixed; reviewer skips/quota notices are not approvals."
  "2026-10-27T08:27:08.886Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 blocker is valid: immutable historical decisions must depend on facts captured at publication, never on mutable current registry meaning. Audit covers milestone capture/parser/fingerprint, shared ownership ledger, correction read/append/recovery, generation and selection diagnostics, SDK and standalone/host JSON/TOON, packed consumers and non-git trackers. Plan: persist fingerprint-bound publication eligibility for new captures, give legacy records their released fixed semantics, and keep current roles only for live Unreleased selection. Existing correction identities and historical snapshots must remain readable and unchanged. Branch already contains current main; no merge needed. No additional concrete inline findings were supplied."
  "2026-10-27T08:44:41.798Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 class fix: schema-2 milestones freeze SDK-classified doneItemIds inside the fingerprint at capture. Ownership and correction replay never consult current custom roles; schema-1 retains released SDK-default semantics and original fingerprints. Live Unreleased eligibility is separate per item, and generation plus selection diagnostics share one predicate; explicit status filters override it. Whole-package audit found and fixed both historical attribution and historical rendering/diagnostics. Behavioral revert proofs each fail with AssertionError when reverting only (1) createReleaseMilestone to the old producer (schema 1 versus expected 2), (2) resolveTrackerReleaseLedger to current-role interpretation (v1 steals v2), or (3) the status predicate to default name filtering (published wording disappears). Sources restored byte-for-byte. Focused related suite 48 passed; final publication regression file 5 passed, zero failures/skips/cancels. Seed 0x291f2 runs 500 registry/JSON/TOON/older-producer-replay sequences with SDK-read correction/native state. A fixture emitted by the released main producer proves legacy read, round trips, correction append/replay and immutable bytes. Dense arrays, duplicates, foreign IDs, hidden properties, non-finite values and a maximum-length sparse array refuse before side effects; oversized eligibility refuses before JSON conversion."
  "2026-10-27T08:54:04.445Z",codex-agent,"Final legacy compatibility also preserves released canonical-token behavior: uppercase CLOSED remains published, padded closed does not become retroactively published. The expanded released-producer fixture and all five publication tests pass. The initial packed registry-drift run stopped at npx because npm registry metadata timed out before command execution (ETIMEDOUT), not because of a product refusal. The final archive run adds schema-1 correction-chain JSON/TOON reads across every launcher and prefers the public dependency cache already populated by its fresh installs; all refusal assertions remain strict. Real-data validation remains 202 items, 189 done-role items, 2 corrections, replay zero, chain 2, 28 unchanged native fields and 15130 identical historical bytes."
  "2026-10-27T09:06:12.246Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passed: 112 checks, 6 installation modes, 8 launcher paths (npm/Bun global, both global host aliases, npm/Bun project-local, npx, bunx), 64 wrong-release JSON/TOON refusals, 9 linked schema-2 corrections and 1 retained schema-1 correction after role promotion/demotion. Every launcher reads both legacy and new chains; exact replays append nothing. npm/npx used the public dependency cache offline with fresh install prefixes after registry/installer timeouts; Bun used its real installers. Behavioral assertions and the production audit gate are unchanged. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint, whitespace, main-history prefix and privacy checks pass. Related focused suite 48 passed; final publication file 5 passed, zero failures/skips/cancels; linked pm test passed. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun CI with at most two workers is the remaining verification. Final-head run URL and measured counts are maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Releasing both claims with items unclosed for orchestrator verification; no additional concrete review finding remains unaddressed."
  "2026-10-27T09:15:18.080Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40478487612 executed all 932 tests successfully on both Node 22 and 26, zero failures/skips/cancellations, but the unchanged 100 percent branch gate refused at 99.96 percent overall (milestones.ts 99.57 percent). Bun and runtime smokes were therefore skipped and are not counted as passes. Inspecting the one missing validation branch and adding an adversarial input case; product thresholds and assertions remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T09:19:03.082Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up is test-only: schema-2 items values undefined, null, a non-array object and a null row now explicitly require typed milestone_invalid refusals. Isolated LCOV reproduced the missing raw-items branch at milestones.ts line 129 with zero hits before; after the added cases all four line-129 branch entries have positive hits. The linked full publication file passes all 5 tests with zero failures/skips/cancels. Product source, generated package files, strict assertions and coverage thresholds are unchanged, so the 112-check packed evidence remains applicable. Pushing this test/evidence follow-up for the full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates; final run URL/counts remain authoritative in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291."
  "2026-10-27T09:50:19.182Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI handoff under the queue wait rule: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40480602451 verifies code/test commit efc023c3d8cf5108f0f57b1219448f54224904f1. At the handoff check both Node 22 and Node 26 jobs remained queued with no steps executed; npm/Bun release gates and direct runtime smokes are pending, not passes. Automatic Actions did not appear for this commit, so the existing CI workflow was dispatched manually. Stopping the wait within 30 minutes after the final code/test push; the orchestrator pipeline owns remaining verification. Prior run 40478487612 executed 932 tests per runtime with zero test failures but failed the unchanged branch threshold; the isolated missing branch is now covered by malformed-items cases, and the linked full publication file passes all 5 tests. Product/package source is unchanged by this handoff. Local 48-test focused set, 5 publication regressions, 112 packed checks across 6 installs/8 launchers, three behavioral revert proofs, real-data counts and history/privacy evidence remain recorded above. Both claims remain released, both items unclosed, no merge or release performed. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291 records the final pending run and counts honestly."
  "2026-10-27T10:08:48.877Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 rule: admission, closure disposition, repair-evidence classification, breaking/semver decisions, diagnostics and output counts must use the same SDK-derived or frozen status meaning. The supplied blocker is valid: literal closed checks let a captured custom done-role duplicate issue appear as Fixed. Whole-package audit includes closure-policy helpers and all generator consumers, SDK/CLI/host, JSON/TOON/document/summary/export/audit, audience contracts and upgrades, packed installers and non-git trackers. Merged main release 2026.10.27 first; resolved only the generated source-map conflict by rebuilding. No additional concrete inline finding was supplied. Plan: propagate one explicit status context, preserving capture-time semantics for history and configured SDK roles for live inputs; never rewrite frozen rows or native metadata."
  "2026-10-27T10:58:45.403Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 class implementation is complete: ChangelogStatusContext carries configured SDK roles plus capture-time per-item meaning through admission, terminal disposition filtering, neutral issue evidence, grouping/prose, breaking/semver, lint, claim audit and exclusion counters. Native statuses/rows are never rewritten. Audience contracts/upgrades and live host/standalone export/generation now load and forward SDK registry context; explicit IDs/aliases normalize both sides through one SDK-backed function. Omitted non-change captures refuse correction view/append before writes, while native history remains intact. Existing 165 closure tests plus three new tests pass (168 total); closure-policy.ts is measured 100 percent lines/branches/functions locally. Seed 0x291f3 executes 500 sequences across eight real SDK registry configurations, aliases including constructor, whitespace/CRLF variants, JSON/TOON captures, SDK-read native state and all projection policies. Four behavioral revert proofs fail independently when reverting only non-change filtering, neutral issue gating, non-category grouping propagation, or correction target eligibility; source restored byte-for-byte."
  "2026-10-27T10:58:53.691Z",codex-agent,"SDK observation, not a blocker and no upstream change filed: a real non-git probe using pinned SDK 2026.10.24 creates a closed Issue with close_reason Duplicate, but the same create call with configured custom done status delivered returns close_reason null and rejects completedAt with the message that it requires a terminal create status. Supported SDK update persists the reason correctly; test fixtures use that path and assert the value read back through SDK before exercising generation. This is reported for owner follow-up rather than re-implementing core behavior."
  "2026-10-27T11:21:21.220Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 related SDK/host/export/audience/upgrades/correction/ownership/publication cohort passes all 51 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"seeded|500|1000\" test/extension.test.ts test/audience-contracts.test.ts test/consumer-upgrades.test.ts test/release-corrections.test.ts test/release-publication.test.ts test/release-ownership.test.ts. The linked three-test custom-role suite also passed via pm test --run --only-last --progress. Existing tests and full CI models remain intact; no separate lint script exists, and typecheck, test typecheck and docstring checks pass."
  "2026-10-27T11:23:23.077Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 real-data validation passed on the filesystem-read-only public origin/main tracker plus disposable non-git overlay: 202 items, 189 SDK-normalized done-role items, 202 milestone members, two corrections created, exact replay zero, chain length two, 25 unchanged native fields. Historical output remains exactly 15130 bytes with SHA256 d2b5ec65c64e3e79d15796486a78a211a900624a0bc45ce4f7e06bd2f5f7411e; source tree is byte-identical. The validator selects an actually rendered claim through the shared generator, rather than an arbitrary done row. Existing main and prior-handoff history prefixes remain byte-identical; new history streams have no main predecessor. Added-content privacy checks pass."
  "2026-10-27T11:27:37.824Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 code/test commit dca4cb01ad8d0a1f923d6d40fbccf0940afc4ca8 is pushed. Full npm/Bun CI for Node 22 and 26 is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40496167954; CodeQL is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40496167971. A duplicate manual dispatch was canceled after automatic CI appeared, preserving runner resources; that cancellation is not gate evidence. The prior-round run 40480602451 ultimately passed 932 tests and all configured coverage dimensions before refusing changelog freshness when main advanced to release 2026.10.27; this round merged that main release and regenerated the changelog, whose local check passes. Packed round-3 acceptance remains in progress; no pending check is counted as a pass."
  "2026-10-27T11:33:20.186Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 packed acceptance completed successfully: node scripts/accept-release-corrections.ts passes all 168 checks across 6 fresh installation modes and 8 launchers (npm-global, npm-global-host, bun-global, bun-global-host, npm-local, bun-local, npx, bunx). Includes all previous 112 assertions, 64 typed wrong-release refusals, 56 closure-role checks across document/summary/semver/diagnostics and JSON/TOON non-change correction refusals, 9 linked new-schema corrections plus 1 retained legacy-schema correction after role changes, zero replay appends. Uses actual installed binaries and native non-git SDK state; npm/npx use cached public dependencies offline, Bun uses real installers. Product/package files are unchanged after the tested archive was built. No concrete review finding remains open; final external JSON/stdin alias regression is being added without weakening any test."
  "2026-10-27T11:37:53.519Z",codex-agent,"Final external-input regression passed: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"host and standalone generation\" test/closure-status-roles.test.ts (1 pass, zero failures/skips/cancels). It covers file and stdin JSON with explicit tracker root, SDK aliases including whitespace/CRLF constructor, and file-only SDK defaults. A fifth isolated behavioral revert removes only external-input registry loading while keeping native loading: the same test fails expected item_count 2 versus actual 0. Source restored byte-for-byte and rebuilt; product/package bytes match dca4cb0. Test typecheck passes. Both prior-round CI runtimes ultimately passed 932 tests and configured coverage before the known release-boundary changelog freshness failure; Bun was skipped, not passed. Round-3 full gates remain queued."
  "2026-10-27T11:48:35.240Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 bounded CI handoff: final code/test and main-integration commit a75007962ec888c1be874e959e8a3a6f616634be is pushed. At 2026-10-27 11:47:55 UTC both Node 22 and Node 26 jobs at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40498185138 remained queued with zero steps executed: npm/Bun full release gates and direct runtime smoke have zero completed gates and no pass counts. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40498185769 remains pending. Superseded queued runs were canceled to conserve capacity, never counted as passes. Stopping within the 30-minute CI wait limit after the implementation push; the orchestrator pipeline owns remaining verification. Local evidence is complete: 168 focused closure tests, 51 related tests, 3 linked custom-role tests, the expanded external-input test, 500 new role/alias sequences, 168 packed checks over 6 installs/8 launchers, five isolated behavioral revert proofs, unchanged historical bytes and 25 native fields on the public-copy validation. Current main tracker evidence is merged, changelog freshness passes, and main/prior history prefixes and added-content privacy pass. Local health has no history-drift warning; it reports the known 32 legacy provenance events and an untracked pm-github extension host-version skew (pinned 2026.10.24 versus extension 2026.10.27), which is not a clean-checkout CI pass. Both own claims are released and both items remain unclosed. No additional concrete review finding was supplied; skipped/budget-exhausted reviewers are not approvals. Product/package bytes are identical to dca4cb0; only tests, main tracker evidence and handoff metadata follow it. No merge or release performed."
  "2026-10-27T14:33:51.524Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 invariant: release ownership derives only from a claim actually published by that capture, never merely from terminal/done membership. An omitted non-change or query-filtered capture owns nothing and cannot suppress a later repair. First published wording and capture-time eligibility remain immutable under reopening, recapture and status-role changes. Every repair must appear exactly once in its first eligible captured window; correction view/append must resolve that same owning claim and report correction_missing only for a selector without a published claim. Whole-package audit covers the shared ledger, frozen/live generation, correction view/append/recovery, SDK/CLI/host, JSON/TOON, contracts/upgrades and packed non-git consumers. Plan: derive claim admission through the shared producer selection policy using frozen eligibility, preserve existing schema records, and exercise 500 random per-item lifecycles over 2-4 releases plus native SDK correction state. Prove failures with only this fix reverted and with only capture-time role meaning reverted. Main is current; prior finished work is retained."
  "2026-10-27T14:58:10.165Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 implementation uses visibleChangelogItems as the ledger publication oracle, with immutable per-capture eligibility. Non-change/query/empty-title omissions own nothing; generation and correction commands consume the same claims. Frozen omission diagnostics are retained separately and cannot shadow a later repair or duplicate item IDs. Added a real native-SDK state machine with 500 independently seeded item lifecycles spanning 2-4 releases: every non-change disposition, reopen/repair, query filters, custom done/active/canceled roles changed before and after publication, JSON/TOON/older-input replays, native field readback and linked correction accessibility. Added dedicated empty-title and actual host/standalone non-git regressions. Local static source and test typechecks pass; no package code has been executed locally under the updated isolation rule. Bubblewrap and user-namespace probes are denied by the host. Focused tests, mutation proofs in disposable copies and then unchanged-threshold full gates will run on credential-free disposable GitHub runners; checkout credentials are not persisted. The preceding round final CI run 40499289077 has now succeeded on both runtimes; current-round evidence remains separate."
  "2026-10-27T15:24:46.741Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 static validation is complete: source typecheck, test/script typecheck, generated build, workflow YAML/embedded-JavaScript syntax, whitespace, main/prior history-prefix and added-content privacy checks pass. Runtime evidence remains pending in the disposable CI runner; no local PR-code execution was used because namespace isolation is denied. The focused job executes both linked pm tests, the existing role/publication/ownership regressions, two behavioral mutants of the 500-native-lifecycle property, the restored fixed property, all 256 packed checks (retaining the prior 168 plus 88 independent later-repair checks), artifact SHA512 stability and fresh read-only public-tracker validation. Full Node 22/26 npm+Bun release gates depend on that focused job and retain the original thresholds and two-worker limit. Checkout credentials are not persisted; test and npm children receive a positive environment allowlist. Prior baseline run 40499289077 passed 935 tests in each of four npm/Bun gates with all configured coverage dimensions 100 percent and both runtime smokes; those are prior-head results, not this round. PM links and runtime commands are recorded; final exact-head URLs, actual counts and revert receipts are maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Both own claims are being released while items remain unclosed for verification."
  "2026-10-27T15:35:30.782Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 source commit 8b9b3a9a1b4db16d9f06b28ef6c6d701d928fffe is pushed; its isolated focused/full CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40530946215 and CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40530945844 are queued, with no runtime pass claimed. The final test-only follow-up counts only non-change dispositions actually written through the SDK and adds a final post-publication role edit plus fresh history/correction reads for all 500 models, including last-release owners. Product/package bytes are unchanged. Claims remain released and items unclosed. Latest exact-head run, actual mutant failures/fixed-model receipt, refreshed public-copy measurements and packed/full-gate counts are maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. No additional concrete inline review finding was supplied; all known instances use the shared publication selector."
  "2026-10-27T15:54:23.878Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 bounded CI handoff: at 2026-10-27 15:52:22 UTC, exact code/test head 299646dc7fec42913d6a15be64ec6802bb034633 still had only the lifecycle job queued with zero executed steps at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40532517260. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40532517257 was also queued. Current-head runtime tests, both behavioral revert receipts, restored-model pass, 256 packed checks, refreshed public-copy measurements, docstring/changelog checks and npm/Bun gates are pending, not passes; the requested new lifecycle/revert evidence is not yet proven. Local source/test/script typechecks, build, workflow syntax, privacy and append-only prefix checks pass. Prior-head run 40499289077 separately passed 935 tests in each of four npm/Bun gates at 100 percent configured coverage, both runtime smokes and CodeQL. Prior measured public-copy baseline remains 202 items, 189 done-role items, 202 milestone members, two corrections, replay zero, chain two, 25 unchanged native fields, 15130 historical bytes with SHA256 d2b5ec65c64e3e79d15796486a78a211a900624a0bc45ce4f7e06bd2f5f7411e; refreshed measurements are pending. Stopping within the existing 30-minute CI cutoff; the orchestrator pipeline owns remaining execution. Following handoff metadata does not change product or tests and requires its own fresh exact-head checks, linked in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Both own claims are already released and both items remain unclosed. No merge or release performed."
  "2026-10-28T15:37:36.857Z",codex-agent,"CI follow-up for upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1615: review passed, but detached-checkout linked-test trust refuses unchanged branch-authored commands unless both testing.allow_untrusted_linked_tests and the existing --allow-untrusted-linked-tests flag are enabled. Merged current main first, including its release and toolchain updates; the generated source-map conflict was resolved by rebuilding. Change scope is the lifecycle workflow only: set the trust opt-in through pinned pm config against the disposable checkout tracker before running linked tests. The setting will not be committed or enabled in the separate release-gate jobs. Add the upstream issue link and removal condition beside the workaround. Tests and product behavior remain unchanged; validate the configuration transition in a disposable detached worktree and wait at most 30 minutes for fresh exact-head lifecycle CI."
  "2026-10-28T15:43:45.219Z",codex-agent,"Targeted detached-worktree validation passed using the main-inherited pinned SDK 2026.10.25: the unchanged linked lifecycle test first exits with trust_refusal, then exits successfully after pm config set untrusted-linked-test-execution enabled. This documented CLI policy alias writes testing.allow_untrusted_linked_tests; the dotted key spelling is not accepted by the pinned config CLI. The existing --allow-untrusted-linked-tests run flag remains required. Configuration was changed only in the disposable worktree, which was removed afterward; the package tracker config is unchanged. The four-line workflow addition is confined to lifecycle and includes https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1615 plus the requested removal condition. Product/test files are unchanged from merged main integration. Source typecheck, workflow/embedded-JavaScript syntax and whitespace checks pass. Final lifecycle CI evidence will be recorded in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291."
